<p>Venezuela’s National Assembly unanimously approved a new (limited) amnesty law meant to speed the release of hundreds of people jailed in cases tied to political turmoil, and to end related court proceedings. Several outlets say acting president Delcy Rodríguez has signed the measure into law, creating a legal path for eligible detainees to leave prison once authorities put it into practice. The law’s limits are at the center of the dispute. It excludes people prosecuted or convicted of promoting military action against Venezuela, a carve-out that reports say could include Nobel Peace Prize winner María Corina Machado, whom the ruling party has accused of calling for international intervention. Human rights groups and other critics say the bill is still too narrow to address the full scope of political detentions, while supporters call it a step toward reconciliation and legal closure after years of unrest. For many families, the immediate stakes are simple: reunions. NGOs and media reports say Venezuela has already freed about 450 political prisoners under U.S. pressure, but that hundreds more remain behind bars.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/r1my1eUcpFUzzgk9XONTlM8FiWnyCmMjLc1E7AdlMaTgRmtT2IfliPkouLHAZ72UGBHQyHvNMhofWmPmDltNPqlZwQtIyTys1IWM8XIzmV0T-YTU6jXjptHUaKRZ0FhSw5WMhndcpXDEUenzzh5UIOpelOHSvQGMi2oBsYxGMxl-mqm7' alt='Relatives of political prisoners embrace outside the Bolivarian National Police Zona 7 prison in Caracas on Feb. 19, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Who could benefit: Reports say the amnesty could cover politicians, activists, lawyers and other detainees held for political reasons.</li><li>Prisoner numbers: Foro Penal has said more than 600 political prisoners remained jailed even after about 450 releases linked to U.S. pressure.</li><li>Time period covered: Lawmakers said the measure spans political-crisis episodes from 2002 to 2025, with the goal of speeding releases and dismissing cases.</li><li>External leverage: The New York Times reported that the bill followed heavy pressure from President Trump’s administration, which shaped the timing of its passage.</li><li>Debate atmosphere: Ahead of the vote, lawmakers described the National Assembly debate as tense as it weighed a sweeping amnesty proposal.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Venezuelan government and ruling party lawmakers: Officials and allied lawmakers said the law is meant to speed releases and close court cases connected to political-crisis episodes. (<a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/02/20/venezuela-passes-unanimous-amnesty-law-excluding-armed-actions-and-serious-crimes'>MercoPress</a>)</li><li>Human rights organizations: Rights groups said the law is limited and does not offer relief for many people still considered political prisoners. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/venezuela-legislature-passes-limited-amnesty-bill-critiqued-by-rights-groups'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Some critics of the bill: The New York Times reported that some critics called the legislation “unjust,” despite the prospect of releases, and raised concerns about its implications. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/world/americas/venezuela-amnesty-bill-prisoners.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Opposition-linked figures: Coverage highlighted that the exclusion for those accused of promoting military action could encompass figures such as María Corina Machado, whom the ruling party has accused of urging international intervention. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-passes-amnesty-law-for-political-prisoners/a-76051759'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-passes-amnesty-law-for-political-prisoners/a-76051759'>Venezuela passes amnesty law for political prisoners</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/20/venezuelan-parliament-unanimously-passes-amnesty-law_6750678_4.html'>Venezuelan parliament unanimously passes amnesty law</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/world/americas/venezuela-amnesty-bill-prisoners.html'>Venezuela Passes Amnesty Bill Denounced by Some as ‘Unjust’</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3344082/venezuela-approves-amnesty-law-could-free-hundreds-political-prisoners'>Venezuela approves amnesty law that could free hundreds of political prisoners</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/venezuela-approves-amnesty-bill-paving-way-for-release-of-hundreds-of-political-detainees'>Venezuela approves amnesty bill, paving way for release of hundreds of political detainees</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/02/20/venezuela-passes-unanimous-amnesty-law-excluding-armed-actions-and-serious-crimes'>Venezuela passes unanimous amnesty law, excluding armed actions and serious crimes</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/venezuela-legislature-passes-limited-amnesty-bill-critiqued-by-rights-groups'>Venezuela legislature passes limited amnesty bill critiqued by rights groups</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/venezuelas-national-assembly-set-resume-tense-debate-sweeping-130303539'>Venezuela’s National Assembly set to resume tense debate on a sweeping amnesty bill</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/one-must-know-how-to-receive-forgiveness-venezuelan-parliament-passes-amnesty-law-13981814.html'>&#x27;One must know how to receive forgiveness&#x27;: Venezuelan parliament passes amnesty law</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/venezuela-approves-amnesty-bill-that-could-see-release-of-hundreds-detained-for-political-reasons/article70654549.ece'>Venezuela approves amnesty bill that could see release of hundreds detained for political reasons</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.np